3.4 9‑Formulation Design of Experiments (DoE)

The Phase 1 matrix systematically varies the three key components to identify optimal synergies. All formulations maintain hemp at 60% and total binder (lime + pozzolan) at 25%, while trading off PCM and aerogel within a fixed additive envelope.

Formulation ID PCM (wt%) Aerogel (wt%) Lime/Pozzolan Ratio Primary Objective
F1 (Control) 0 0 100:0 Baseline hempcrete properties
F2 5 2 90:10 Low PCM, standard aerogel
F3 8 2 90:10 Baseline HTBC (target architecture)
F4 12 2 90:10 Maximum latent heat, check strength retention
F5 8 0 90:10 PCM only, no aerogel
F6 8 4 90:10 Enhanced aerogel for stretch λ goal
F7 8 2 80:20 High pozzolan for moisture resistance
F8 5 4 80:20 Optimise for lowest λ + adequate PCM
F9 10 2 80:20 Higher PCM with improved binder

Each formulation is replicated three times for every test method, yielding 27 distinct data points per measured property. Statistical analysis (ANOVA) identifies significant main effects and interactions, guiding Phase 2 refinement.

