📋 SOP-01: RAW MATERIAL CHARACTERIZATION & QUALIFICATION

Objective
Verify incoming material specifications before formulation to ensure batch‑to‑batch reproducibility.

Materials

· Hemp hurd (particle size 2–10 mm, moisture <12%)
· Hydrated lime (Ca(OH)₂, purity ≥95%, D50 <15 µm)
· Microencapsulated PCM (core: capric‑lauric eutectic or paraffin C18; shell: PMMA/melamine; Tmelt 22–26°C)
· Silica aerogel granules (hydrophobic, bulk density 80–150 kg/m³, particle size 1–3 mm)
· Pozzolan/clay additive (optional, SiO₂+Al₂O₃ ≥70%)

1. Hemp Hurd Quality Check

1. Weigh 100 g sample (±0.01 g), record mass (m_dry_initial).
2. Dry at 105°C for 24 h in ventilated oven.
3. Re‑weigh (m_dry_final). Calculate moisture content:
      MC (%) = [(m_dry_initial – m_dry_final) / m_dry_initial] × 100
4. Acceptance: MC ≤ 12%. If >12%, pre‑dry batch before use.
5. Sieve analysis (2 mm, 5 mm, 10 mm screens). Record mass fractions.
6. Document particle size distribution (PSD) curve.

2. Lime Binder Purity & Reactivity

1. Perform acid‑neutralization titration (ASTM C25):
   · Dissolve 1.000 g lime in 50 mL 1N HCl.
   · Back‑titrate excess acid with 1N NaOH, phenolphthalein indicator.
   · Calculate Ca(OH)₂ % = [(V_HCl – V_NaOH) × N × 37.04] / sample_mass
2. Acceptance: Ca(OH)₂ ≥ 93%.
3. Optional: CO₂ uptake rate test (TGA under 10% CO₂ flow).

3. PCM Microcapsule Validation

1. DSC scan (–10°C to 50°C, ramp 5°C/min, N₂ purge):
   · Record melting onset, peak, enthalpy (ΔH_melt).
   · Acceptance: Tmelt = 22–26°C; ΔH_melt ≥ 120 J/g (core basis).
2. Thermal cycling stability (pre‑screen):
   · Cycle 10× between 15°C and 35°C (10 min dwell each).
   · Re‑run DSC; acceptance: ΔH loss ≤ 5%.
3. Shell integrity check:
   · Disperse 1 g PCM in 50 mL ethanol, sonicate 5 min.
   · Filter, evaporate supernatant, weigh residue.
   · Acceptance: leakage < 2 wt%.

4. Aerogel Granule Characterization

1. Bulk density: Fill 100 mL graduated cylinder, tap 100×, record mass/volume.
2. Hydrophobicity test: Drop 0.1 g granules on water surface; acceptance: float >30 min.
3. Particle size distribution (laser diffraction, dry dispersion): D50 = 1.5–2.5 mm; span <1.5.
4. Thermal conductivity screening (transient hot‑wire on loose granules): λ ≤ 0.022 W/m·K.

Documentation: Complete Form TS-FRM-001 (Raw Material Certificate of Analysis). Attach DSC curves, PSD plots, titration logs.

