📋 SOP-02: FORMULATION MIXING & SAMPLE CASTING

Objective
Produce homogeneous HTBC mixtures with controlled PCM/aerogel dispersion.

Target Formulation (Baseline v1.0)

Component Mass Fraction Function
Hemp hurd (dry) 60.0% Structural matrix, carbon sink
Hydrated lime 25.0% Binder, carbonation curing
Water 10.0% Workability, hydration
Pozzolan (optional) 5.0% Early strength, durability
Microencapsulated PCM 8.0% Latent heat storage
Silica aerogel granules 2.0% Nano‑insulation reinforcement

PCM and aerogel added post‑initial mixing to minimize shear damage.

Equipment

· Twin‑shaft planetary mixer (stainless steel, variable speed)
· Ultrasonic homogenizer probe (20 kHz, titanium tip)
· Precision balances (±0.1 g for batch >5 kg)
· Molds: 160×40×40 mm prisms (mechanical), 300×300×30 mm panels (thermal)

Phase A: Bio‑Matrix Pre‑Mix

1. Pre‑weigh all dry components (hemp, lime, pozzolan) into mixer bowl.
2. Mix dry at 60 rpm for 3 min to homogenize.
3. Add 80% of water gradually over 2 min while mixing at 90 rpm.
4. Scrape bowl walls, continue mixing 2 min at 120 rpm.
5. Check workability: slump test (target 120–180 mm).
   · If too stiff: add remaining water in 0.5% increments.
   · If too fluid: add 1% lime filler.

Phase B: PCM Integration (Low‑Shear)

1. Reduce mixer speed to 40 rpm.
2. Pre‑warm PCM to 28°C (above Tmelt) to reduce viscosity.
3. Add PCM gradually over 90 sec while mixing.
4. Mix additional 90 sec at 40 rpm — DO NOT exceed 60 rpm (shell rupture risk).
5. Visual check: uniform color distribution, no visible PCM pooling.

Phase C: Aerogel Dispersion (Ultrasonic‑Assisted)

1. Transfer 10% of batch to ultrasonic vessel for pilot dispersion test:
   · Add aerogel granules to slurry.
   · Sonicate: 30% amplitude, 5 sec ON / 2 sec OFF, total 60 sec.
   · Check dispersion under stereomicroscope (10×).
2. If pilot passes (no agglomerates >5 mm), proceed to full batch:
   · Add aerogel to main mixer at 30 rpm.
   · Simultaneously apply probe sonication to mixing zone (20% amplitude, pulsed).
   · Mix 3 min total.
3. Final homogeneity check: extract 3 subsamples, measure density variation. CV ≤ 5%.

Phase D: Casting & Initial Curing

1. Lubricate molds with food‑grade silicone release agent.
2. Pour mixture in 2–3 layers, rod each layer 25× to eliminate voids.
3. Vibrate mold at 50 Hz for 30 sec.
4. Cover with breathable cellulose film.
5. Initial cure: 24 h at 20±2°C, RH 60±5%.
6. Demold gently; label samples (batch ID, timestamp, formulation code).

Critical Control Points

Step Parameter Tolerance Action if Out‑of‑Spec
A.5 Slump 120–180 mm Adjust water ±0.5%; retest
B.4 Mixer speed ≤60 rpm Stop; inspect PCM integrity
C.3 Density CV ≤5% Re‑mix batch; review sonication protocol
D.5 Initial cure RH 60±5% Adjust chamber; document deviation

Documentation: Complete Form TS-MIX-002 (Batch Record & Dispersion Log). Attach photos of dispersion quality and slump test.

