12.7 Evaluation Methodology

Step 1: Initial Screening (Mandatory Gates)
Check all "Mandatory? Yes" criteria. Any failure = disqualification unless supplier provides corrective action plan with confirmed delivery date.

Step 2: Technical Scoring
Assign each remaining criterion a score: 1 (Poor) to 5 (Excellent) based on provided evidence and sample test results. Multiply by category weights, sum to get weighted score (max 5.0). Convert to percentage (score/5 * 100).

Step 3: Commercial & Sustainability Score

· Commercial (30% weight of final): Price competitiveness, lead time, payment terms, volume flexibility. Score 1–5.
· Sustainability (20% weight of final): Environmental certifications, carbon footprint transparency, circular economy practices. Score 1–5.

Step 4: Final Ranking
Final Score = 0.5 × Technical Score + 0.3 × Commercial Score + 0.2 × Sustainability Score. Minimum approval threshold: 70/100.

Step 5: Sample Qualification Testing
For suppliers passing paper evaluation, request sample (1–5 kg). Perform full qualification per SOP‑01 criteria and integrate results into technical score before final contract.

